{\*\ftnsep\chftnsep}\pgndec\pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Intro}{
 [00:00:04\u8211\'9600:00:37]\line Welcome to The Lighter Side of the Spectrum, the podcast that celebrates the multiple hats we wear and the juggling acts we perform in life. Whether you're parenting kids and teens on the autism spectrum, navigating the ever-evolving healthcare industry, or building a more inclusive and impactful world, this is your space to find connection, inspiration, and growth. Together, we'll share stories, tackle challenges, and explore how innovation and inclusion create better outcomes for everyone. Because no matter the spectrum, there's always a lighter side. Now here's your host, David Koffer.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:00:37\u8211\'9600:00:59]\line Hi everyone, welcome to a special edition of The Lighter Side of the Spectrum. I am David Koffer. I'm with my friend Kim Kretich, and we're wrapping up a really amazing 3-day experience. It's an inclusive surf camp officially called the Resonance Surf Camp. But Kim, this was initially your brainchild a few years ago.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Kim Kredich}{
 [00:00:59\u8211\'9600:02:01]\line Yeah, we had started coming with our 3 sons, one of whom was diagnosed with autism back in 2001. So we started coming to IndoJack Surf School, and then we just kept coming and kept coming. And finally, we\u8212\'97 I invited all these families for whom I advocated, kids of all abilities and their siblings, to make it a truly inclusive surf camp. And we did that 2016, '17, and '18. And then we, and then unfortunately our son Ben was killed by an impaired driver in August of 2023.\line And so many people reached out to the IndoJack Surf Charity to donate in memory of Ben that we did another Surf camp. And, uh, and I think it sort of helped fund the entire season for Indo Jack's surf charities. And then the Peyton Project said, let's take\u8212\'97}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:02:01\u8211\'9600:02:03]\line Great foundation based in Tennessee.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Kim Kredich}{
 [00:02:03\u8211\'9600:02:21]\line In Tennessee that promotes all types of communication, uh, specifically for Peyton, the letterboard, spelling to communicate. And so they said, We loved it. We want to continue it through the foundation. And so that's exactly what they did. And if you turn around, you can see\u8212\'97}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:02:21\u8211\'9600:02:22]\line There we go.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Kim Kredich}{
 [00:02:22\u8211\'9600:03:00]\line There it is. There's the Resonance Surf Camp. And that's actually a silhouette of Ben surfing. He had a great surfing style where he'd just sort of go like that and then start flapping his legs because it felt like\u8212\'97 Felt like he was flying. He always said that. So yeah, it was just amazing to have this continue. And especially have such a unique perspective on communication and brain-body disconnect and to connect with the ocean and surfing and with all the supports that anyone would need. It's been really remarkable.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:03:00\u8211\'9600:03:06]\line It's so great. I mean, and, you know, every surfer had their own instructor with them out there.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Kim Kredich}{
 [00:03:07\u8211\'9600:03:08]\line At least one.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:03:08\u8211\'9600:03:26]\line At least one, right? Sometimes more. I mean, we had all ages, we had all abilities, you know, different levels of experience. But the level of support is just unprecedented from the instructors and from the families. I mean, that's what really struck me. I mean, that's what I'm going to leave here with.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Kim Kredich}{
 [00:03:26\u8211\'9600:04:00]\line Yeah, it was originally just this understanding that you can be truly inclusive with all the supports that you need. And I always tied it to inclusion in the schools. That was the big sort of analogy of, hey, with accommodations, modifications, support, you can include. And so that's just, especially with families hanging out together and hanging out for dinner, not just on the beach, but\u8212\'97}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:04:00\u8211\'9600:04:00]\line Right.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Kim Kredich}{
 [00:04:00\u8211\'9600:04:15]\line It just, everyone belonged. And that's always been the spirit of the inclusive surf camp. It was called Pushing into the Swell, and now it's called the Resonance Surf Camp. And it's in honor of, it's in honor of Ben. And it just, this feels great.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
