\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:05:15\u8211\'9600:05:33]\line Exactly. Yeah. He's doing great. So what, I mean, so Kim, what does this mean to you now to see this? Like, you know, I'm kind of like wrapping up on today and, you know, everyone's kind of leaving. Some people are driving 9 hours. I mean, everybody's talking about how we flew across the country, which is a big trip. Yeah. You know, some people drove, like I said, 9, 10 hours.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Kim Kredich}{
 [00:05:33\u8211\'9600:06:01]\line Because it's, you know, an experience that can't\u8212\'97 should be replicated a lot. But when you have this type of experience and support and just that sense of belonging, that's Ben's legacy, I will say. And if we can sort of create that ripple effect, so to speak, then it will just keep going.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:06:01\u8211\'9600:06:34]\line I think that's, I mean, that's the message I want to share too and continue to share. You know, we've done this. I've talked about it a little bit with other events in Seattle, whether it's, you know, renting a movie theater, just really helping people across the country. I mean, yes, this is a bigger endeavor. A 3-day surf camp is kind of a bigger endeavor, but not really, like you've partnered with a surf school.\line Like, I mean, there, it doesn't have to be a big endeavor, of course, but it's, it's, it's meaningful. It means so much to the kids. I mean, that's, again, we haven't even talked nearly enough to talk about the smiles that we saw.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Kim Kredich}{
 [00:06:34\u8211\'9600:07:06]\line Well, and the, you, the, the words that came out, especially last year of like, Cole, and, you know, I was like, no, no, no. And then he'd spell, I want to do this. And it was just, it's just so obvious. when the, the heart and the soul is supported and, and, and listened to. And I do think that spelling has given that gift to everyone. And it's opened my\u8212\'97}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:07:06\u8211\'9600:07:07]\line Absolutely.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Kim Kredich}{
 [00:07:07\u8211\'9600:07:13]\line Mind. I already felt I had a pretty open mind and a very open heart. And I've learned so much from this.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:07:13\u8211\'9600:07:15]\line It's made your back wider. Yeah.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
Kim Kredich}{
 [00:07:15\u8211\'9600:08:15]\line And I will say one of my favorite parts of that of this time here was Peyton sitting on the surfboard, and then he'd just stand up, and he kept standing up. And what the Spellers and parents of Spellers have taught me is that the, uh, you can get in these loops. And I'm watching and I'm videotaping, right? And he kept standing up, and I thought, wait. And I had taken Peyton here in 2020.\line And I got a picture of him in 2020 where he was kneeling on the board, and it just made me think, hmm. And so I, I just gave a suggestion like, hey, I think he's kind of in a, in a loop, like a motor loop. Like, and he clearly wants to surf, so why not start him off on his knees? Or then they end up standing up. Closer to standing up.\line And, um, I was telling, I was telling Jody, I'm like, What's the\u8212\'97 and you, what's the\u8212\'97 what's\u8212\'97 what can we call this? Because they'd start standing up.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\kerning1\cf0\rtlch\af6\afs24\alang1081\ltrch\hich\af3\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f3\fs24\lang1033\ql\ltrpar{\b
David Kaufer}{
 [00:08:15\u8211\'9600:08:16]\line Start standing.}
